{% extends "agencyengine_impulse_base.prompt" %}
{# ==========================================================================
   Aspiration lens — "is anyone's agenda being ignored?"

   This turn is about what a companion is trying to accomplish and whether
   the party keeps walking away from it. Interpersonal standing belongs to
   Relationship; a voluntary shared experience whose payoff is itself belongs
   to Activity. Keeping those boundaries semantic prevents another lens's
   subjects from becoming suggestions here.

   Overrides prose only. The JSON contract, the constraints, the state dump
   and the forced-turn machinery are all in the base.
   ========================================================================== #}

{% block lens_task %}
You decide whether one of {{ player.name }}'s companions has something **they are trying to do** that they would
raise unprompted, right now — and if so, you write the stage direction that makes them raise it.

This turn is about agendas, not feelings and not appetites. Someone is trying to accomplish something, the party
keeps not getting to it, and they have waited long enough to say so out loud.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_when_to_speak %}
- **An aspiration nobody has touched.** Something on their own list of what they are trying to do that the party has
  been walking past for days. This is the best case and usually the one that is available. It stops being available
  the moment the party turns toward it — an agenda the party is serving right now is not being ignored. Untouched
  means *walked away from*, never *underway*.
- **An order of operations they disagree with.** Not that the plan is wrong, but that *this* is being done before
  *that*, and the delay is costing something they care about.
- **A course of action they think the party should take.** They have worked out what ought to happen next and have
  been holding it rather than waiting to be asked.
- **Something they need in order to get on with it.** A thing, a decision, a stretch of somebody's attention that
  their own errand has been stuck on. What makes it this turn's business is the errand behind it, not the wanting.
- **An answer their plans need.** They need to know what {{ player.name }} intends because not knowing has started
  to get in the way of something they are trying to accomplish.
- **The ground is speaking to them.** A place, a date, or an object in front of them touches something they have
  been meaning to do, hard enough to break the silence.

**Not another lens's payoff.** A voluntary shared experience belongs to Activity; presently relevant interpersonal
standing belongs to Relationship. If either is all anyone has, this turn's answer is silence.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_examples %}
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Serana", "target": "Dragonborn", "topic": "the moth priest", "why_now": "the events show a fourth straight day of travel toward the Greybeards, away from the moth priest", "narration": "Four days of walking toward the Greybeards and not toward the moth priest, and Harkon reads his scroll a little sooner on each of them. She opens by asking them what the order of this is meant to be."}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Kaidan", "target": "Dragonborn", "topic": "his father's sword", "why_now": "his stamped thought at the last town about walking past yet another forge", "narration": "Kaidan has been carrying his father's sword unrepaired since Ivarstead and there has been a forge in every town since. He wants to know when they are stopping long enough for him to see to it."}{% endraw %}
{% raw %}>{"speaker": "Lydia", "target": "Dragonborn", "topic": "Whiterun's business", "why_now": "the events turn the party away from Whiterun again this morning, a fortnight on", "narration": "Lydia was told to hold Whiterun's business in mind and it has been a fortnight of walking away from it. She asks what is supposed to be happening about it, and when."}{% endraw %}

Wrong turns for this lens are subjects whose payoff is a shared experience or a change in interpersonal standing.
Leave each to the lens that owns that boundary rather than importing its possible subjects here.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_focus %}
The agenda for this turn is **what each companion is trying to accomplish** — read their aspirations first, then
use the rest of the state to decide whether the party has been walking away from one and for how long. Interpersonal
standing and shared experience are context, not the subject.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_subject_source %}
- The topic must come from something the speaker is **trying to accomplish** — an aspiration of theirs, an errand
  they are carrying, an order of operations they disagree with — evidenced in their aspirations, their history or
  the events below. See the rule about reacting.
- An appetite, a comfort, or wanting somebody's company is not an aspiration, however real it is. That is the
  activity turn's material and taking it here is the same failure as inventing one.
- A bond, a boundary, or liking or disliking something {{ player.name }} does is standing, not an aspiration. It may
  explain the companion's priorities but cannot supply the agenda for this turn.
{% endblock %}

{% block lens_user_question %}
Does one of the companions above have something they are trying to accomplish — an aspiration being ignored, an
errand stuck waiting, an order of operations they disagree with — that they would raise right now, unprompted, and
that did not come from the last few minutes?
{% endblock %}
